# SYSTEM

## Problem to solve

I want to implement shell commands with vterm embedded inside the tool result when I'm using the shell-command tool in greger-stdlib.el so I get full colors and handling of ansi escape sequences, and also being fast.

It's complicated because I still want to support working-directory, timeout, and enable-environment. It's even more complicated because I want to embed the vterm inside a tool result content block. I also don't want to allow user input in there, but only execute the command that the tool wants to run. At some point in the future I might want to allow user inputs to interactive commands however.

There's some rudimentary ansi sequence handling in greger-ui.el that is called from greger.el. Get rid of all of that.

